hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1159","Ali bin Khashram told us, Isa, meaning Ibn Yunus, told us, and Yusuf bin Musa, Abdullah bin Numayr Al-Hamdani, told us all, about Imran bin Zaida bin Nashit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Khaled Al-Walbi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah: “When he got up at night, he would raise He raised his voice at times and lowered it at times, and he used to remember that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.”"
"1160","We are told by Abdullah bin Hashem, we are told by Abdul Rahman, meaning Ibn Mahdi, on the authority of Muawiyah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Qais, and Bahr Bin Nasr, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Muawiyah bin Salih told me, that Abdullah bin Abi Qais told him, that he asked Aisha: How was the recitation of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, at night? Was he recited aloud or silently? She said: “He did all of that, sometimes out loud and sometimes secretly.” Bahr added more to his speech, saying: So I said: “Praise be to God, who has made the matter expansive.”"
